<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theoretical Proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Proposition 1</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(x)=\mathbb{E}[Z(x,y)\mid x],\quad\Sigma_{w}=\mathbb{E}_{x}[\operatorname{Cov}(Z(x,y)\mid x)],\quad\Sigma_{b}=\operatorname{Cov}_{x}(\mu(x))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(x)=\mathbb{E}[Z(x,y)\mid x],\quad\Sigma_{w}=\mathbb{E}_{x}[\operatorname{Cov}(Z(x,y)\mid x)],\quad\Sigma_{b}=\operatorname{Cov}_{x}(\mu(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}Z(x_{i},G_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j=1}^{m}Z(x_{i},G_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since completions within a prompt are conditionally independent given <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(G_{i}\mid x_{i})=\frac{1}{m}\operatorname{Cov}(Z(x_{i},y)\mid x_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(G_{i}\mid x_{i})=\frac{1}{m}\operatorname{Cov}(Z(x_{i},y)\mid x_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the law of total covariance to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(G_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{x}[\operatorname{Cov}(G_{i}\mid x_{i})]+\operatorname{Cov}_{x}(\mathbb{E}[G_{i}\mid x_{i}])=\frac{1}{m}\Sigma_{w}+\Sigma_{b}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(G_{i})=\mathbb{E}_{x}[\operatorname{Cov}(G_{i}\mid x_{i})]+\operatorname{Cov}_{x}(\mathbb{E}[G_{i}\mid x_{i}])=\frac{1}{m}\Sigma_{w}+\Sigma_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since prompts are sampled independently, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g})=\frac{1}{n}\operatorname{Cov}(G_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g})=\frac{1}{n}\operatorname{Cov}(G_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=B/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=B/m</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g})=\frac{m}{B}\!\left(\frac{1}{m}\Sigma_{w}+\Sigma_{b}\right)=\frac{1}{B}\Sigma_{w}+\frac{m}{B}\Sigma_{b}.\qed" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g})=\frac{m}{B}\!\left(\frac{1}{m}\Sigma_{w}+\Sigma_{b}\right)=\frac{1}{B}\Sigma_{w}+\frac{m}{B}\Sigma_{b}.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Corollary 1</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Proposition 1, for any allocation <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nm=B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nm=B</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g})=\frac{1}{B}\Sigma_{w}+\frac{m}{B}\Sigma_{b}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g})=\frac{1}{B}\Sigma_{w}+\frac{m}{B}\Sigma_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Consider any two allocations <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}&lt;m_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}&lt;m_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with the same budget <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. Their difference is</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{2}})-\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{1}})=\frac{m_{2}-m_{1}}{B}\,\Sigma_{b}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{2}})-\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{1}})=\frac{m_{2}-m_{1}}{B}\,\Sigma_{b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{b}=\operatorname{Cov}_{x}(\mu(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{b}=\operatorname{Cov}_{x}(\mu(x))</annotation></semantics></math> is a covariance matrix, it is positive semidefinite, so for any vector <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\bigl(\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{2}})-\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{1}})\bigr)v=\frac{m_{2}-m_{1}}{B}\,v^{\top}\Sigma_{b}\,v\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\bigl(\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{2}})-\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{1}})\bigr)v=\frac{m_{2}-m_{1}}{B}\,v^{\top}\Sigma_{b}\,v\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{2}})\succeq\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{2}})\succeq\operatorname{Cov}(\hat{g}_{m_{1}})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}&gt;m_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}&gt;m_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, meaning the variance of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}</annotation></semantics></math> in every gradient direction is non-decreasing in <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. The minimum is thus attained at <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, giving <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=B</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Pseudocode for POISE</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> POISE</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Prompt distribution <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>; initial policy <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>;
initial value estimator <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{f_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{f_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>; prompt batch size <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>;
value-buffer size <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>; PPO clip <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\leftarrow f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\leftarrow f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, value buffer <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{V}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{V}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> step <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1,2,\ldots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1,2,\ldots,T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathrm{old}}\leftarrow\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathrm{old}}\leftarrow\theta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              Sample a mini-batch of prompts <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{b}\}_{b=1}^{M}\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{b}\}_{b=1}^{M}\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{V}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{V}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each prompt <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
               Sample
<math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y_{b}^{(1)},y_{b}^{(2)}\overset{\mathrm{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(\cdot\mid x_{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em">.</mo></mrow></mover><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{b}^{(1)},y_{b}^{(2)}\overset{\mathrm{i.i.d.}}{\sim}\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(\cdot\mid x_{b})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
               Extract internal state features
<math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{b}^{(i)}\leftarrow\phi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(x_{b},y_{b}^{(i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{b}^{(i)}\leftarrow\phi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}(x_{b},y_{b}^{(i)})</annotation></semantics></math>
for <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> via forward hooks.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
               Compute rewards <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{b}^{(i)}\leftarrow R(x_{b},y_{b}^{(i)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{b}^{(i)}\leftarrow R(x_{b},y_{b}^{(i)})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
               Compute cross-rollout baselines:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
              
<math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{b}^{(1)}\leftarrow g_{f}\bigl(\phi_{b}^{(2)}\bigr),\quad b_{b}^{(2)}\leftarrow g_{f}\bigl(\phi_{b}^{(1)}\bigr)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{b}^{(1)}\leftarrow g_{f}\bigl(\phi_{b}^{(2)}\bigr),\quad b_{b}^{(2)}\leftarrow g_{f}\bigl(\phi_{b}^{(1)}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
               Compute advantages
<math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{b}^{(i)}\leftarrow r_{b}^{(i)}-b_{b}^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{b}^{(i)}\leftarrow r_{b}^{(i)}-b_{b}^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
               Add policy-update examples:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
              
<math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\mathcal{R}\cup\bigl\{\bigl(x_{b},y_{b}^{(i)},A_{b}^{(i)}\bigr)\bigr\}_{i=1,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\mathcal{R}\cup\bigl\{\bigl(x_{b},y_{b}^{(i)},A_{b}^{(i)}\bigr)\bigr\}_{i=1,2}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
               Add value-estimator examples:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
              
<math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{V}\leftarrow\mathcal{S}_{V}\cup\left\{\bigl(\phi_{b}^{(1)},r_{b}^{(2)}\bigr),\bigl(\phi_{b}^{(2)},r_{b}^{(1)}\bigr)\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{V}\leftarrow\mathcal{S}_{V}\cup\left\{\bigl(\phi_{b}^{(1)},r_{b}^{(2)}\bigr),\bigl(\phi_{b}^{(2)},r_{b}^{(1)}\bigr)\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
              Update <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> by maximizing the PPO objective in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In PPO-style policy update. ‣ 3.2 Policy Optimization with Cross-Rollout Baselines ‣ 3 Policy Optimization with Internal State Value Estimation (POISE) ‣ Your Language Model is Its Own Critic: Reinforcement Learning with Value Estimation from Actor’s Internal States" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) on <math id="alg1.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
              
              Update <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> by minimizing

<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{(\phi,\widetilde{r})\in\mathcal{B}_{V}\cup\mathcal{S}_{V}}\bigl(g_{f}(\phi)-\widetilde{r}\bigr)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{(\phi,\widetilde{r})\in\mathcal{B}_{V}\cup\mathcal{S}_{V}}\bigl(g_{f}(\phi)-\widetilde{r}\bigr)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
              
              
              Append <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{V}</annotation></semantics></math>; evict examples older than <math id="alg1.l21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> steps.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l22.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Baseline Algorithm</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We adopt DAPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite> as our baseline RL algorithm.
For each prompt <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, a group of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> responses
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{o^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{o^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled from the old policy <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and the following objective is optimized:</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{DAPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>DAPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{DAPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(q,a)\sim\mathcal{D},\,\{o^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>o</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(q,a)\sim\mathcal{D},\,\{o^{(i)}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot\mid q)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E15Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Bigg[\,\frac{1}{\sum_{i=1}^{G}|o^{(i)}|}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\sum_{t=1}^{|o^{(i)}|}\min\!\Big(\,r_{t}^{(i)}(\theta)\,\hat{A}_{t}^{(i)},\;\mathrm{clip}\!\big(r_{t}^{(i)}(\theta),\,1-\varepsilon_{\text{low}},\,1+\varepsilon_{\text{high}}\big)\hat{A}_{t}^{(i)}\Big)\Bigg]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.428em;" width="1.428em"><mi>clip</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>low</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Bigg[\,\frac{1}{\sum_{i=1}^{G}|o^{(i)}|}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\sum_{t=1}^{|o^{(i)}|}\min\!\Big(\,r_{t}^{(i)}(\theta)\,\hat{A}_{t}^{(i)},\;\mathrm{clip}\!\big(r_{t}^{(i)}(\theta),\,1-\varepsilon_{\text{low}},\,1+\varepsilon_{\text{high}}\big)\hat{A}_{t}^{(i)}\Big)\Bigg],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{s.t.}\quad 0\;&lt;\;\big|\{\,o^{(i)}\mid\mathrm{is\_equivalent}(a,o^{(i)})\,\}\big|\;&lt;\;G," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>is</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>equivalent</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{s.t.}\quad 0\;&lt;\;\big|\{\,o^{(i)}\mid\mathrm{is\_equivalent}(a,o^{(i)})\,\}\big|\;&lt;\;G,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the importance ratio and the group-relative advantage are</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{t}^{(i)}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(o_{t}^{(i)}\mid q,o_{&lt;t}^{(i)})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(o_{t}^{(i)}\mid q,o_{&lt;t}^{(i)})},\qquad\hat{A}_{t}^{(i)}=\frac{R^{(i)}-\mathrm{mean}(\{R^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{G})}{\mathrm{std}(\{R^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{G})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>mean</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>std</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{t}^{(i)}(\theta)=\frac{\pi_{\theta}(o_{t}^{(i)}\mid q,o_{&lt;t}^{(i)})}{\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(o_{t}^{(i)}\mid q,o_{&lt;t}^{(i)})},\qquad\hat{A}_{t}^{(i)}=\frac{R^{(i)}-\mathrm{mean}(\{R^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{G})}{\mathrm{std}(\{R^{(j)}\}_{j=1}^{G})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">DAPO augments GRPO with four key techniques:
(i) <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clip-Higher</span> decouples the lower and upper clipping bounds
(<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\text{high}}&gt;\varepsilon_{\text{low}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>low</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\text{high}}&gt;\varepsilon_{\text{low}}</annotation></semantics></math>), giving low-probability tokens
more room to be promoted and mitigating entropy collapse;
(ii) <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dynamic Sampling</span> filters out prompts whose responses are all correct
or all incorrect, ensuring that every batch yields effective gradients;
(iii) <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Token-Level Policy Gradient Loss</span> normalizes by the total token count
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}|o^{(i)}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}|o^{(i)}|</annotation></semantics></math> rather than per-sequence, so longer responses contribute proportionally
to the loss;
(iv) <span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overlong Reward Shaping</span> applies a length-aware penalty to truncated
samples to reduce reward noise.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike the original DAPO, we drop the length penalty and use a purely binary reward based solely on correctness for simplicity:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{(i)}\;=\;\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }o^{(i)}\text{ is correct},\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is correct</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{(i)}\;=\;\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }o^{(i)}\text{ is correct},\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Value Estimator</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Hidden states used for estimator training are collected from the model’s teacher-forced
log probability forward pass, which is already required by our policy optimization algorithm and therefore does not need additional computation. Specifically, the
implementation registers a forward hook on one transformer layer during this log probability
computation, and pools prompt hidden states and reasoning hidden states separately.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ B.3 Value Estimator ‣ Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ Your Language Model is Its Own Critic: Reinforcement Learning with Value Estimation from Actor’s Internal States" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> lists the hyperparameters used by
the hidden-state value estimator. The prompt and reasoning hidden-state features
are obtained by mean-pooling the last <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> prompt tokens and the last <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>
reasoning tokens, respectively. For a pair of rollouts
<math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y^{(1)},y^{(2)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y^{(1)},y^{(2)})</annotation></semantics></math> from the same prompt, the supervised target for the feature
row of <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the paired rollout reward
<math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{R}^{(i)}=R(x,y^{(j)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{R}^{(i)}=R(x,y^{(j)})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T4.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A2.T4.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A2.T4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:144.9pt;">
<span id="A2.T4.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T4.3.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Component</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A2.T4.3.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_tt">
