<td id="A5.T9.5.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.25pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A5.T9.5.15.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">27</span></td>
<td id="A5.T9.5.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.25pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A5.T9.5.15.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.139</span></td>
<td id="A5.T9.5.15.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.25pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A5.T9.5.15.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.292</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Pooling window.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also vary the number of final tokens used for mean pooling while fixing the layer to 19. As shown in Table <a href="#A5.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Pooling window. ‣ E.1 Ablations of Hyperparameters During Hidden State Extraction ‣ Appendix E Ablations ‣ Your Language Model is Its Own Critic: Reinforcement Learning with Value Estimation from Actor’s Internal States" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, last-10 and last-15 pooling perform almost identically, while last-5 pooling is weaker. We choose last-10 pooling as the default because it achieves the best Pearson correlation while using a shorter extraction window than last-15.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Pooling-window ablation for Qwen3-4B at layer 19.</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T10.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T10.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T10.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.35pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A5.T10.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Pooling window</span></td>
<td id="A5.T10.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.35pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A5.T10.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">MAE <math id="A5.T10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A5.T10.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.35pt 5.0pt;"><span id="A5.T10.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Pearson <math id="A5.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A5.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
